.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ID \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the ID of the owner.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RestoreStatus \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the restoration status of an object. Objects in certain storage classes must be restored before they can be retrieved. For more information about these storage classes and how to work with archived objects, see \fI\%Working with archived objects\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets. Directory buckets only support \fBEXPRESS_ONEZONE\fP (the S3 Express One Zone storage class) in Availability Zones and \fBONEZONE_IA\fP (the S3 One Zone\-Infrequent Access storage class) in Dedicated Local Zones.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
IsRestoreInProgress \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies whether the object is currently being restored. If the object restoration is in progress, the header returns the value \fBTRUE\fP . For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqtrue\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the object restoration has completed, the header returns the value \fBFALSE\fP . For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqfalse\(dq, RestoreExpiryDate=\(dq2012\-12\-21T00:00:00.000Z\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the object hasn\(aqt been restored, there is no header response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RestoreExpiryDate \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates when the restored copy will expire. This value is populated only if the object has already been restored. For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqfalse\(dq, RestoreExpiryDate=\(dq2012\-12\-21T00:00:00.000Z\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Name \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The bucket name.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Prefix \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Keys that begin with the indicated prefix.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- For directory buckets, only prefixes that end in a delimiter (\fB/\fP ) are supported.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Delimiter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Causes keys that contain the same string between the \fBprefix\fP and the first occurrence of the delimiter to be rolled up into a single result element in the \fBCommonPrefixes\fP collection. These rolled\-up keys are not returned elsewhere in the response. Each rolled\-up result counts as only one return against the \fBMaxKeys\fP value.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- For directory buckets, \fB/\fP is the only supported delimiter.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
MaxKeys \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Sets the maximum number of keys returned in the response. By default, the action returns up to 1,000 key names. The response might contain fewer keys but will never contain more.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
CommonPrefixes \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
All of the keys (up to 1,000) that share the same prefix are grouped together. When counting the total numbers of returns by this API operation, this group of keys is considered as one item.
.sp
A response can contain \fBCommonPrefixes\fP only if you specify a delimiter.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBCommonPrefixes\fP contains all (if there are any) keys between \fBPrefix\fP and the next occurrence of the string specified by a delimiter.
.sp
\fBCommonPrefixes\fP lists keys that act like subdirectories in the directory specified by \fBPrefix\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For example, if the prefix is \fBnotes/\fP and the delimiter is a slash (\fB/\fP ) as in \fBnotes/summer/july\fP , the common prefix is \fBnotes/summer/\fP . All of the keys that roll up into a common prefix count as a single return when calculating the number of returns.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- For directory buckets, only prefixes that end in a delimiter (\fB/\fP ) are supported.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- When you query \fBListObjectsV2\fP with a delimiter during in\-progress multipart uploads, the \fBCommonPrefixes\fP response parameter contains the prefixes that are associated with the in\-progress multipart uploads. For more information about multipart uploads, see \fI\%Multipart Upload Overview\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for all (if there are any) keys between Prefix and the next occurrence of the string specified by a delimiter. CommonPrefixes lists keys that act like subdirectories in the directory specified by Prefix. For example, if the prefix is notes/ and the delimiter is a slash (/) as in notes/summer/july, the common prefix is notes/summer/.
.sp
Prefix \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the specified common prefix.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
EncodingType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Encoding type used by Amazon S3 to encode object key names in the XML response.
.sp
If you specify the \fBencoding\-type\fP request parameter, Amazon S3 includes this element in the response, and returns encoded key name values in the following response elements:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDelimiter, Prefix, Key,\fP and \fBStartAfter\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBurl\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
KeyCount \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBKeyCount\fP is the number of keys returned with this request. \fBKeyCount\fP will always be less than or equal to the \fBMaxKeys\fP field. For example, if you ask for 50 keys, your result will include 50 keys or fewer.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ContinuationToken \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If \fBContinuationToken\fP was sent with the request, it is included in the response. You can use the returned \fBContinuationToken\fP for pagination of the list response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
NextContinuationToken \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBNextContinuationToken\fP is sent when \fBisTruncated\fP is true, which means there are more keys in the bucket that can be listed. The next list requests to Amazon S3 can be continued with this \fBNextContinuationToken\fP . \fBNextContinuationToken\fP is obfuscated and is not a real key
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
StartAfter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If StartAfter was sent with the request, it is included in the response.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RequestCharged \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If present, indicates that the requester was successfully charged for the request. For more information, see \fI\%Using Requester Pays buckets for storage transfers and usage\fP in the \fIAmazon Simple Storage Service user guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrequester\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
